## Cloud Network Endpoints
In cloud computing architectures (like [AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-endpoint-types.html) or [IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/cloud-object-storage?topic=cloud-object-storage-endpoints)), endpoints represent routing destinations for internet traffic: [20, 21, 22] 

* Public Endpoints: Accessible directly from anywhere on the public internet.
* Private Endpoints: Strictly restricted to internal Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs); hidden from the public internet.
* Edge-Optimized Endpoints: Route traffic through global content delivery network (CDN) edge locations to lower latency.
* Regional Endpoints: Intended for traffic originating from within the exact same geographical cloud region. [20, 21, 23] 

------------------------------
## Clinical Trial Endpoints (Medical Science)
In medicine and clinical research, an endpoint refers to the target outcome used to measure if a treatment works: [24, 25, 26, 27] 

* Primary Endpoints: The single most critical outcome evaluated in a study to judge a drug's success (e.g., survival rate).
* Secondary Endpoints: Additional outcomes monitored to provide secondary data (e.g., side effects or quality of life).
* Surrogate Endpoints: Lab values or physical signs used as a substitute for a true clinical endpoint (e.g., lowering blood pressure as a surrogate for preventing heart attacks). [24, 28, 29, 30] 

